---
// src/pages/security.astro
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Security Overview — VerseSEO"
  description="Learn how VerseSEO protects your account, website data, and infrastructure. Our approach to security, data handling, and responsible disclosure."
  canonical="https://verseseo.com/security"
>
  <Navbar />

  <main class="flex-1">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16 sm:py-20">
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 tracking-tight mb-2">Security Overview</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 mb-10">Last updated: August 28, 2026</p>

      <div class="prose prose-slate prose-sm max-w-none space-y-8 text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 mt-8 mb-3">Account Security</h2>
          <p>VerseSEO takes account security seriously. Our approach includes:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 mt-2 space-y-1">
            <li><strong>Password storage</strong> — Passwords are hashed using industry-standard cryptographic techniques. Plaintext passwords are never stored.</li>
            <li><strong>Session management</strong> — Session tokens are stored securely and communicated over encrypted connections.</li>
            <li><strong>Email verification</strong> — New accounts require email verification to confirm identity.</li>
            <li><strong>Password reset</strong> — Password reset flows use time-limited, single-use tokens sent to your registered email.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">If you suspect unauthorized access to your account, contact us immediately at <a href="mailto:support@verseseo.com" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">support@verseseo.com</a>.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 mt-8 mb-3">Website Scan Data</h2>
          <p>When you submit a URL for analysis, VerseSEO crawls the target website to collect technical SEO, content, and visibility data. Here's how we handle that data:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 mt-2 space-y-1">
            <li>Scan data is stored in association with your account and project.</li>
            <li>We do not share your scan results with third parties.</li>
            <li>You can delete your projects and associated scan data at any time from your account settings.</li>
            <li>When your account is deleted, we take reasonable steps to remove or anonymize personal information in accordance with our <a href="/privacy" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 mt-8 mb-3">Infrastructure</h2>
          <p>VerseSEO is built on modern, managed infrastructure:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 mt-2 space-y-1">
            <li><strong>Frontend hosting and delivery</strong> — Cloudflare</li>
            <li><strong>Database</strong> — Managed PostgreSQL (Neon)</li>
            <li><strong>Payment processing</strong> — DodoPayments (PCI-compliant payment handling)</li>
            <li><strong>Email delivery</strong> — Resend (transactional emails only)</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">These providers are contractually obligated to protect your data and may not use it for purposes other than providing services to VerseSEO. For full details, see our <a href="/privacy" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 mt-8 mb-3">Data Transmission</h2>
          <p>All data transmitted between your browser and VerseSEO's servers is encrypted using TLS (Transport Layer Security). This includes account credentials, form submissions, API requests, and scan data.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 mt-8 mb-3">Third-Party Services</h2>
          <p>VerseSEO integrates with third-party APIs to provide search and visibility data, including Google Search Console, Brave Search, Apify, Reddit, and Google Gemini. These services are used solely to deliver functionality within the product. We do not sell, rent, or share your data with these providers beyond what is necessary to operate the Service.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 mt-8 mb-3">Data Retention and Deletion</h2>
          <p>We retain your data for as long as necessary to provide the Service and maintain your account. You can:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 mt-2 space-y-1">
            <li>Delete individual projects and their associated scan data from your account dashboard.</li>
            <li>Request full account and data deletion by contacting <a href="mailto:support@verseseo.com" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">support@verseseo.com</a>.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">When accounts are deleted, we take reasonable steps to remove or anonymize personal information, except where retention is required for legal or legitimate business purposes.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 mt-8 mb-3">Analytics</h2>
          <p>VerseSEO uses Google Analytics 4 to collect anonymized usage data. Google Analytics uses cookies to collect traffic data. You can opt out via the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">Google Analytics Opt-Out Browser Add-on</a>.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">Essential cookies required for authentication and session management are also used. You can manage cookie preferences through the <a href="#" id="security-cookie-pref-link" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">Cookie Preferences</a> link in the footer.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 mt-8 mb-3">Reporting Security Concerns</h2>
          <p>If you discover a security vulnerability or have a security concern related to VerseSEO, please report it to <a href="mailto:support@verseseo.com" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">support@verseseo.com</a>. Please include:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 mt-2 space-y-1">
            <li>A description of the issue</li>
            <li>Steps to reproduce the vulnerability</li>
            <li>Any relevant screenshots or logs</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">We will review your report and respond as quickly as possible. We ask that you do not publicly disclose vulnerabilities until we have had a chance to investigate and address the issue.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 mt-8 mb-3">Limitations</h2>
          <p>While we implement reasonable technical and organizational safeguards, no method of transmission or storage is completely secure. We cannot guarantee absolute security. If you have questions about our security practices, contact us at <a href="mailto:support@verseseo.com" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">support@verseseo.com</a>.</p>
        </section>

      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<script>
  const cookieLink = document.getElementById('security-cookie-pref-link');
  cookieLink?.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
    e.preventDefault();
    window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('open-cookie-preferences'));
  });
</script>
